  "notes": [
    "Backtest only: 2025 CVEs scored with information available at their publication month, checked against later KEV additions. This is NOT an estimate of 2026 accuracy; there are no 2026 labels.",
    "Few positives: fold 1 has 52 exploited CVEs in its test pool and fold 2 has 32, so one hit is about 2% (fold 1) to 3% (fold 2) of all positives. Read every number with its interval.",
    "The top-500 difference between 'ours' and 'exploit_then_epss' is not robust: it changes sign between folds and seed sets, and its paired bootstrap interval (seed set 0) includes 0. 'ours' ranks better on AUC in both folds, but that interval also includes 0 for seed set 0.",
    "'ours' = C1 (HGB on exploit signals + assigner KEV history + masked description text score), trained with time-safe labels (KEV additions only up to the train end). Values are medians over 5 seed sets; top500_seed_range is [lowest, highest] over the seed sets; ci95 for 'ours' is from seed set 0.",
    "'ours_first_pass_optimistic' (fold 1 only) is the first-pass model with train labels that overlap the test period (KEV additions to 2025-12-31). It is optimistic and is shown only for comparison; do not quote it as the result.",
    "top500 and top250 break tied scores by cve_id; top500_tie_range is [worst, best] over all orders of the tied rows and appears only where ties change the count. ci95.top500 is the 95% bootstrap interval of the tie-neutral expected top-500 hits (2000 resamples). median_rank and work_to_catch_50pct use ties by cve_id.",
    "work_to_catch_50pct = how many CVEs from the top of the ranking you must fix to catch half of the exploited ones.",
    "claim_ids name the ledger entry (results/claims_model.json) behind each value; null means no claim exists, so the value must not be published. Check each claim's status before display."
